WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.100
In 1994, The Little Rascals hit theaters...but
wasn't a huge box office hit.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.190
Instead, it became a favorite among millennials
due to frequent airings on cable TV.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.809
It's a sweet, low-key outing, but it’s a
standout because of its cast of delightful

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:13.910
child actors.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:18.070
So, where is the cast of The Little Rascals
now?

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.020
"Otay!"

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.430
Travis Tedford

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:25.760
Previously seen as a tiny pitchman for Welch's
grape juice, Travis Tedford played Spanky,

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.039
leader of the Little Rascals.

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:30.160
After appearing in forgettable movies like
The Thirteenth Floor, Tedford moved back to

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.710
his home state of Texas in 2002, and now works
in marketing for a large credit union.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.120
Brandon “Bug” Hall

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.960
The actor who played the lovelorn Alfalfa
followed up The Little Rascals with appearances

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.100
in films like the aptly-titled The Stupids,
and played Eddie Munster in The Munsters Scary

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.489
Little Christmas.

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:49.239
Bug Hall has continued to work steadily, appearing
on Castle, CSI Miami, and Criminal Minds.

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:53.720
In the 2014 direct-to-DVD The Little Rascals
Save the Day, he has a cameo as an ice cream

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.720
man.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.720
Ross Bagley

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.650
Of all of his co-stars, Ross Bagley, who played
Buckwheat, enjoyed the most high-profile acting

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:00.650
career.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.850
Back when sitcoms brought in cute tykes to
boost ratings, Bagley appeared as Nicky, the

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.100
precocious little kid in The Fresh Prince
of Bel Air.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.580
He co-starred with Will Smith once more in
Independence Day.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:13.130
Bagley later took a break from acting, and
recently earned his degree in film studies.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.340
Brittany Ashton Holmes

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.390
Darla charmed audiences as the object of Alfalfa's
affections, as well as the target of the He-Man

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.840
Woman-Haters Club.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.570
It was Brittany Ashton Holmes' first-ever
role, and has remained her most prominent.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.060
She retired from the screen at the ripe old
age of seven, and is pursuing a degree in

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.670
political science.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.689
Blake McIver Ewing

00:01:31.689 --> 00:01:34.980
Waldo was the villain of The Little Rascals,
as the son of a wealthy oil baron played by

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.100
Donald Trump.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.530
Post-Little Rascals, Blake McIver Ewing voiced
Eugene on Hey Arnold! and hosted The People's

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.530
Couch.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.790
He's also worked with the It Gets Better project,
and funded the recording of an album by working

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.250
as a go-go dancer.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.409
Ewing opted to keep Waldo's amazing hair into
adulthood, which is simply awesome.

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.409
Kevin Jamal Woods

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:55.260
The kid who played Stymie continued acting
sporadically throughout childhood, appearing

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.799
in two distinctly '90s things: He voiced a
puppy in Babe, and guest-starred on Walker,

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:00.939
Texas Ranger.

00:02:00.939 --> 00:02:04.920
These days, Kevin Jamal Woods is an audio
engineer and music producer in Texas.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.130
Zachary Mabry

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:09.429
Porky stole a lot of scenes as Spanky's little
brother and devoted assistant.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.160
It's the only acting Zachary Mabry ever did.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.290
Now, he’s a public sector accountant in
the Dallas area.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.620
Sam Saletta

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.430
If there're a bunch of kids getting into crazy
adventures, you need a bully to bug'em right?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.980
That's Movie Logic 101.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:24.700
Since playing Butch in The Little Rascals,
Sam Saletta has done a lot of voiceover work,

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.910
particularly for Recess, Rocket Power, and
the video game Call of Duty: Black Ops.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:32.230
He's also a singer-songwriter, and played
in a band called Jubala.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.230
Petey the Dog

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:37.430
Petey’s last on-screen credit comes from
a 2012 documentary series called American

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:38.430
Dog.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.620
And considering that The Little Rascals was
released more than 20 years ago, it's safe

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:46.150
to say Petey has since been, uh, sent to a
nice farm upstate where he can run and play

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.150
all day.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.590
Thanks for watching!

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:51.269
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:53.680
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Rascal was your favorite...

